# Stage new files in git

- As soon as you create a new file or module, run `git add` on it.
- Do not leave project sources/tests/resources/Gradle files as `??` untracked.
- After creating or renaming files, check `git status` and stage every new path that belongs to the change.
- Exclude secrets and unrelated local junk; do not stage accidental edits outside the task.
- Staging is not a commit — commit only when the user explicitly asks.
